<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command uses the same algorithm as</span> <span class="Command">Interactive Noise Reduction By Curvature</span><span lang="EN-GB">. The differences are that you cannot reduce the maximum offset of the points and the magnitude of changes is displayed after the filter is done.</span></p>
<p class="Use">Using <span class="Command">Select By Curvature</span> and <span class="Command">Invert Selection</span> you can select the flatter areas and apply any noise reduction filter (like <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Average Noise Reduction</b></span>). But <span class="Command">Noise Reduction By Curvature</span> can perform such task at once.</p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span class="Command">Noise Reduction By Curvature</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to eliminate the noise on the flatter areas and to preserve features.</span></p>
